Committee Secretary: Thank you, Mr. Chair.

14
00:43:50,220 --> 00:43:51,300
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: Thank you, ComSec.

15
00:43:52,160 --> 00:43:58,720
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: The Chair would like to acknowledge the presence of Senator Francis Pangilina. Thank you, sir, for joining us.

16
00:43:59,020 --> 00:43:59,500
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: Thank you.

17
00:44:01,760 --> 00:44:09,460
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: Now, the Chair would like to give his opening statement. Good afternoon to our colleagues here at the Senate, guests, and resource persons, and to the Department of Finance.

18
00:44:09,900 --> 00:44:19,240
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: Today, the Committee on Finance will deliberate the proposed budget of the DOF, its attached agencies, and cooperation for the fiscal year 2027,

19
00:44:19,740 --> 00:44:22,140
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: and discuss relevant points in strengthening our economy.

20
00:44:22,320 --> 00:44:27,640
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: Our revenue efforts, managing debt levels, and expanding our financial resources.

21
00:44:28,560 --> 00:44:36,300
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: The Department of Finance plays a critical role in ensuring that the government has sufficient resources to fund our priorities,

22
00:44:36,900 --> 00:44:44,140
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: from healthcare and education to infrastructure, agriculture, social protection, and other essential services.

23
00:44:45,140 --> 00:44:48,600
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: To fund government programs and projects, revenue collection is critical.

24
00:44:49,360 --> 00:44:52,000
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: Kailangan nating malaman ang improvement sa

25
00:44:52,160 --> 00:44:59,360
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: BIR tax administration, digitalization at enforcement ay talagang nagresulta sa mas mataas na koleksyon,

26
00:45:00,000 --> 00:45:03,640
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: mas maayos na compliance at mas kaunting tax leakages.

27
00:45:04,860 --> 00:45:09,300
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: On the other hand, Bureau of Customs continues to face persistent challenges

28
00:45:09,300 --> 00:45:12,300
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: in combating smuggling and illicit trade.

29
00:45:12,300 --> 00:45:17,000
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: Kaya nais nating malaman sa kabila ng mas mababang budget ngayong taon,

30
00:45:17,680 --> 00:45:19,960
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: kaya ba nating palakasin ang border protection,

31
00:45:20,540 --> 00:45:23,420
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: masugpo ang smuggling at mapataas ang revenue collection.

32
00:45:23,420 --> 00:45:30,300
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: As the government continues to operate within a challenging fiscal environment

33
00:45:30,300 --> 00:45:35,740
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: and as we seek additional revenues, equally important are sound debt management,

34
00:45:36,500 --> 00:45:38,920
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: responsible borrowing, and prudent spending.

35
00:45:39,540 --> 00:45:45,460
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: So in discussing the proposed budget today, we want clear answers on three basic questions.

36
00:45:46,080 --> 00:45:48,360
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: Tama at sapat ba ang ating kinukulekta?

37
00:45:49,180 --> 00:45:52,660
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: Maayos at efficient ba nating ginagamit ang bawat piso?

38
00:45:52,660 --> 00:45:58,480
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: At responsable ba nating pinamamahalan ang ating utang at fiscal obligations

39
00:45:58,480 --> 00:46:01,920
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: upang hindi nating ipasa sa susunod na henerasyon?

40
00:46:02,940 --> 00:46:05,580
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: As our economy and fiscal needs continue to evolve,

41
00:46:05,860 --> 00:46:10,880
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: we must ensure that our country remains in a stable and sustainable fiscal position.

42
00:46:11,740 --> 00:46:15,780
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: And we owe it to the Filipino taxpayers to ensure that every peso requested

43
00:46:15,780 --> 00:46:18,500
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: is a peso efficiently and responsibly spent.

44
00:46:19,240 --> 00:46:20,940
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: Today's hearing gives us an opportunity

45
00:46:20,940 --> 00:46:22,640
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: to examine whether we can achieve a sustainable future

46
00:46:22,640 --> 00:46:26,900
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: and whether our revenue strategies, borrowings, investments,

47
00:46:27,200 --> 00:46:30,740
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: and financing mechanisms are putting us on the right track,

48
00:46:31,080 --> 00:46:33,740
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: not only for the coming year but for the years ahead.

49
00:46:34,680 --> 00:46:35,880
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: Thank you very much.

50
00:46:36,540 --> 00:46:40,900
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: And welcome, Secretary Frederick Go, the Undersecretaries,

51
00:46:41,060 --> 00:46:47,160
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: Treasurer Sharon Almanza, the USECs, ASECs, and the heads of agencies.

52
00:46:47,760 --> 00:46:50,540
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: Welcome to the DOF budget briefing.

53
00:46:50,540 --> 00:46:50,680
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: Thank you.

54
00:46:51,560 --> 00:46:52,540
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: I have worked with a lot of people.

55
00:46:52,640 --> 00:46:54,420
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: Some of you, familiar faces.

56
00:46:54,800 --> 00:46:56,860
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: We have passed a lot of vital measures.

57
00:46:58,280 --> 00:46:59,000
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: Pinagod niyo ako.

58
00:47:00,320 --> 00:47:03,200
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: Ilang measures yun, mga technical, but through your help.

59
00:47:03,840 --> 00:47:05,960
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: Yung si Carlo, yung si Catherine Fong.

60
00:47:06,560 --> 00:47:11,740
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: These are the people that backstop, that make me look good.

61
00:47:11,880 --> 00:47:16,560
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: Kahit nahirap at technical yung mga pinagpapasako, salamat sa inyo.

62
00:47:17,200 --> 00:47:21,700
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: Anyway, I'd like to ask Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan

63
00:47:21,700 --> 00:47:22,620
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: for his opinion.

64
00:47:22,640 --> 00:47:24,220
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: His opening statements, if there's any.

65
00:47:25,120 --> 00:47:29,000
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: I would rather listen to their presentations, Mr. Chairperson.

66
00:47:29,020 --> 00:47:30,700
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: Okay, since there are no more questions,

67
00:47:30,820 --> 00:47:34,240
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: I now call on Secretary Frederick Go to deliver his opening statement

68
00:47:34,240 --> 00:47:38,060
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: and to present the 2027 proposed expenditure program

69
00:47:38,060 --> 00:47:40,980
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: of the Department of Finance and its attached agencies and corporations.

70
00:47:41,760 --> 00:47:42,320
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: The floor, sir.

71
00:47:43,520 --> 00:47:47,520
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: Thank you, Chairperson Senator JV Ejercito,

72
00:47:47,520 --> 00:47:50,400
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: Vice Chairperson, Senator Kiko Pangilinan,

73
00:47:51,280 --> 00:47:52,620
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: Senate Committee Member,

74
00:47:52,640 --> 00:47:54,540
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: members, colleagues in government, good afternoon.

75
00:47:55,060 --> 00:47:57,960
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: Thank you for this opportunity to present the proposed

76
00:47:57,960 --> 00:48:02,380
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: fiscal year 2027 budget of the Department of Finance,

77
00:48:02,760 --> 00:48:05,100
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: its bureaus, and attached agencies.

78
00:48:06,020 --> 00:48:07,860
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: The DOF has a critical mandate,

79
00:48:08,420 --> 00:48:10,280
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: raise resources the government needs,

80
00:48:11,080 --> 00:48:12,560
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: manage them responsibly,

81
00:48:13,060 --> 00:48:15,380
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: and protect the country's fiscal stability.

82
00:48:16,000 --> 00:48:18,040
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: We are the government's fundraiser,

83
00:48:18,660 --> 00:48:21,820
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: but raising revenue is only one part of the job.

84
00:48:22,640 --> 00:48:24,000
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: We also have to manage debt,

85
00:48:24,820 --> 00:48:26,480
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: strengthen financial systems,

86
00:48:27,300 --> 00:48:29,360
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: improve tax and customs administration,

87
00:48:29,840 --> 00:48:32,540
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: and make sure that the government has the fiscal space

88
00:48:32,540 --> 00:48:33,980
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: to fund its priorities.

89
00:48:36,260 --> 00:48:39,280
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: When this administration took office in 2022,

90
00:48:39,460 --> 00:48:42,200
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: the country was carrying 12.79 trillion

91
00:48:42,200 --> 00:48:44,500
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: in national government debt,

92
00:48:45,200 --> 00:48:47,700
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: much of it accumulated during the pandemic.

93
00:48:48,200 --> 00:48:50,780
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: Our task since then has been clear,

94
00:48:51,320 --> 00:48:52,200
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: rebuild fiscal space,

95
00:48:52,640 --> 00:48:54,520
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: while continuing to support growth

96
00:48:54,520 --> 00:48:56,300
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: and invest in the country's future.

97
00:48:57,520 --> 00:48:58,360
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: As a response,

98
00:48:58,500 --> 00:49:02,040
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: we crafted the country's medium-term fiscal framework in 2022,

99
00:49:02,920 --> 00:49:05,900
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: the government's blueprint for reducing our deficit and debt

100
00:49:05,900 --> 00:49:07,600
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: as a percentage of GDP,

101
00:49:08,460 --> 00:49:09,800
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: while creating more jobs,

102
00:49:10,020 --> 00:49:11,380
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: increasing people's incomes,

103
00:49:11,940 --> 00:49:13,480
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: and reducing poverty.

104
00:49:14,200 --> 00:49:18,560
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: It set us on a path of gradual and sustained fiscal consolidation

105
00:49:18,560 --> 00:49:20,860
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: to restore fiscal space,

106
00:49:20,860 --> 00:49:22,620
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: while continuing to invest in the future,

107
00:49:22,620 --> 00:49:24,260
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: while continuing to invest in the foundations of growth.

108
00:49:25,100 --> 00:49:28,780
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: But our recovery has not happened in an easy environment.

109
00:49:29,840 --> 00:49:30,480
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: Over the years,

110
00:49:30,580 --> 00:49:32,780
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: external pressures and global uncertainties

111
00:49:32,780 --> 00:49:34,460
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: have disrupted supply chains

112
00:49:34,460 --> 00:49:36,380
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: and pushed inflation up,

113
00:49:36,740 --> 00:49:38,520
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: affecting the pace of growth.

114
00:49:39,120 --> 00:49:40,300
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: In this context,

115
00:49:40,440 --> 00:49:43,300
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: we needed to recalibrate our growth and fiscal targets

116
00:49:43,300 --> 00:49:45,460
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: to keep them realistic and responsive

117
00:49:45,460 --> 00:49:47,500
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: to evolving economic conditions.

118
00:49:47,980 --> 00:49:50,460
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: But the direction of our fiscal policy

119
00:49:50,460 --> 00:49:51,660
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: has remained consistent.

120
00:49:51,900 --> 00:49:52,600
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: We have been working hard to ensure that

121
00:49:52,600 --> 00:49:54,600
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: we have pursued stronger revenue collection,

122
00:49:55,240 --> 00:49:56,360
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: disciplined expenditure,

123
00:49:57,020 --> 00:49:58,960
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: and prudent debt management.

124
00:50:00,280 --> 00:50:05,360
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: Total revenues have grown by an average of 10.54% annually

125
00:50:05,360 --> 00:50:07,980
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: over the last four years.

126
00:50:09,080 --> 00:50:10,740
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: And in 2025,

127
00:50:11,040 --> 00:50:13,940
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: the BIR surpassed 3 trillion pesos

128
00:50:13,940 --> 00:50:16,420
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: in tax collections for the first time.

129
00:50:17,080 --> 00:50:19,240
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: We continue to strengthen collections

130
00:50:19,240 --> 00:50:21,800
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: while mobilizing additional non-tax revenues

131
00:50:21,800 --> 00:50:22,580
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: and managing the economy.

132
00:50:22,600 --> 00:50:26,600
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: As a result,

133
00:50:26,820 --> 00:50:29,120
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: the fiscal deficit has continued to narrow

134
00:50:29,120 --> 00:50:31,180
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: as we remain on track

135
00:50:31,180 --> 00:50:34,420
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: toward our medium-term consolidation targets.

136
00:50:35,100 --> 00:50:37,300
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: From 8.6% in 2021

137
00:50:37,300 --> 00:50:39,600
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: and 7.3% in 2022,

138
00:50:40,240 --> 00:50:43,100
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: we are bringing it down to 5.4%

139
00:50:43,100 --> 00:50:45,300
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: by the end of 2026.

140
00:50:47,280 --> 00:50:50,440
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: Our debt indicators also remain manageable.

141
00:50:50,440 --> 00:50:51,700
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: In 2025,

142
00:50:51,700 --> 00:50:55,700
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: national government debt stood at 63.2% of GDP

143
00:50:55,700 --> 00:51:00,440
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: while general government debt settled at 56.8% of GDP,

144
00:51:01,060 --> 00:51:04,080
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: well below the 70% international benchmark

145
00:51:04,080 --> 00:51:05,640
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: for debt sustainability

146
00:51:05,640 --> 00:51:08,260
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: and within a manageable range

147
00:51:08,260 --> 00:51:11,120
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: compared with other emerging economies.

148
00:51:11,680 --> 00:51:13,060
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: More importantly,

149
00:51:13,440 --> 00:51:16,140
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: we have maintained a prudent debt mix,

150
00:51:16,780 --> 00:51:17,920
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: predominantly domestic,

151
00:51:18,280 --> 00:51:20,300
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: predominantly carrying fixed interest rates,

152
00:51:20,300 --> 00:51:21,200
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: and predominantly,

153
00:51:21,700 --> 00:51:24,480
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: structured with long repayment terms

154
00:51:24,480 --> 00:51:27,580
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: of at least five years.

155
00:51:28,540 --> 00:51:28,920
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: First,

156
00:51:29,500 --> 00:51:33,020
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: 67% of our debt is domestic.

157
00:51:33,700 --> 00:51:36,620
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: This reduces our exposure to foreign exchange risks

158
00:51:36,620 --> 00:51:39,400
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: while also supporting the continued development

159
00:51:39,400 --> 00:51:41,140
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: of our local capital market.

160
00:51:41,980 --> 00:51:42,260
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: Second,

161
00:51:42,780 --> 00:51:45,620
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: 90% of our debt carries fixed interest rates.

162
00:51:46,020 --> 00:51:47,520
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: This provides greater certainty

163
00:51:47,520 --> 00:51:48,980
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: in our debt servicing costs

164
00:51:48,980 --> 00:51:51,140
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: and shields us from sudden increases

165
00:51:51,140 --> 00:51:51,680
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: or fluctuations

166
00:51:51,700 --> 00:51:53,340
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: in global interest rates.

167
00:51:54,380 --> 00:51:55,020
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: And third,

168
00:51:55,580 --> 00:51:57,860
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: 84.1% of our debt

169
00:51:57,860 --> 00:52:00,020
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: has long-term repayment periods,

170
00:52:00,560 --> 00:52:01,780
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: meaning we have several years

171
00:52:01,780 --> 00:52:03,780
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: before these obligations fall due.

172
00:52:05,440 --> 00:52:07,880
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: These generally refer to debt

173
00:52:07,880 --> 00:52:10,240
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: with maturities of over five years.

174
00:52:11,520 --> 00:52:13,740
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: This longer maturity profile

175
00:52:13,740 --> 00:52:15,720
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: reduces our refinancing risks

176
00:52:15,720 --> 00:52:17,780
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: and gives us greater predictability

177
00:52:17,780 --> 00:52:19,600
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: in managing our debt obligations.

178
00:52:20,460 --> 00:52:21,680
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: This strategic,

179
00:52:21,700 --> 00:52:22,640
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: borrowing mix

180
00:52:22,640 --> 00:52:24,240
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: strengthened our resilience

181
00:52:24,240 --> 00:52:25,260
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: to external shocks

182
00:52:25,260 --> 00:52:27,120
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: and made our debt obligations

183
00:52:27,120 --> 00:52:27,840
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: more predictable

184
00:52:27,840 --> 00:52:28,660
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: and manageable

185
00:52:28,660 --> 00:52:30,080
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: over the long term.

