853
01:15:48,120 --> 01:16:10,580
BOC Commissioner Ariel F. Nepomuceno: But if I may, Your Honor, recognizing the complexity of the NSW project, what BOC has done when we came in July last year is to embark on our own, of course, with the support of the Secretary of Finance, Sec. Frederick, we are now embarking on our own customs processing system.

854
01:16:10,580 --> 01:16:13,120
BOC Commissioner Ariel F. Nepomuceno: Paliwanag ko lang po ng konti briefly.

855
01:16:13,820 --> 01:16:22,940
BOC Commissioner Ariel F. Nepomuceno: CPS will remove the human intervention involved in the processes of the importations.

856
01:16:22,940 --> 01:16:30,440
BOC Commissioner Ariel F. Nepomuceno: Ganito po yan. We have identified 15 ICT projects. At the center of this is the CPS, Customs Processing System.

857
01:16:30,540 --> 01:16:36,380
BOC Commissioner Ariel F. Nepomuceno: Ganito po yan. CPS, if compared to Singapore CPS, they call it NSW.

858
01:16:37,540 --> 01:16:43,440
BOC Commissioner Ariel F. Nepomuceno: Mabilis lang silang gumawa ng NSW na, which they were able to easily compel.

859
01:16:43,820 --> 01:16:51,200
BOC Commissioner Ariel F. Nepomuceno: We have identified 15 other agencies dealing with the Singapore Customs to cooperate with the Singapore Customs NSW.

860
01:16:51,860 --> 01:17:03,620
BOC Commissioner Ariel F. Nepomuceno: Now that we have our own SW, which is not being led by BOC, what we did is to embark with our own CPS, which will be similar to the NSW.

861
01:17:04,260 --> 01:17:06,820
BOC Commissioner Ariel F. Nepomuceno: Ganito po yan. So lahat ng merong...

862
01:17:07,340 --> 01:17:08,160
BOC Commissioner Ariel F. Nepomuceno: Yes, sir.

863
01:17:09,160 --> 01:17:09,580
BOC Commissioner Ariel F. Nepomuceno: Yes, sir.

864
01:17:09,580 --> 01:17:13,580
BOC Commissioner Ariel F. Nepomuceno: But we have to prioritize and we should not be...

865
01:17:13,820 --> 01:17:18,240
BOC Commissioner Ariel F. Nepomuceno: dependent on the NSW per se because that's not within our full control.

866
01:17:18,820 --> 01:17:27,280
BOC Commissioner Ariel F. Nepomuceno: What our CPS will do once we roll this out middle of next year is to prioritize, for example, agencies such as the Department of Agriculture,

867
01:17:28,340 --> 01:17:40,260
BOC Commissioner Ariel F. Nepomuceno: the, well, FDA sana, but FDA also has some issues, PNP, DTI, yung mga mabilis na ho nating isama.

868
01:17:40,260 --> 01:17:43,300
BOC Commissioner Ariel F. Nepomuceno: So the data will be automatic real time.

869
01:17:43,820 --> 01:17:44,840
BOC Commissioner Ariel F. Nepomuceno: From the...

870
01:17:44,840 --> 01:17:55,860
BOC Commissioner Ariel F. Nepomuceno: With the complete loop from the submission of the import documents or, of course, export documents, assessment, payment after releasing, including, Your Honor, the bank documents.

871
01:17:56,320 --> 01:18:06,200
BOC Commissioner Ariel F. Nepomuceno: We have to include the bank documents because, of course, we assume that the banks will never collude with the smugglers because they have a bigger name and a stake to protect.

872
01:18:06,360 --> 01:18:13,200
BOC Commissioner Ariel F. Nepomuceno: So with our own CPS, we will be able to approximate what a full NSW can do.

873
01:18:13,820 --> 01:18:43,800
BOC Commissioner Ariel F. Nepomuceno: But the difference is we will just be prioritizing the agencies which are crucial to our operations. Of course, ideally, more than 40 plus agencies should be able to integrate real-time in terms of providing us the permits and all the relevant documents that will be vital in the computations of the values that we will be able to base our collections from and to be able to say yes or no, which importations which will be allowed or not.

874
01:18:43,820 --> 01:19:11,900
BOC Commissioner Ariel F. Nepomuceno: So, yun naman po ang good news. Now, with the question, how are we funding this? Wala po ang choice dahil wala po sa budget yan ng 2026. So, we have started with the PPP proposed to us. Nasa legal and technical discussions na po kami. And we're confident that this can be rolled out with the pilot areas middle of next year, meaning June, July, Your Honor.

875
01:19:11,900 --> 01:19:17,680
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: And what would the pilot areas be? Do you already, have you identified that? Or it's still?

876
01:19:18,500 --> 01:19:35,200
BOC Commissioner Ariel F. Nepomuceno: Yes, sir. But initial lang po yan. We might first try with the Port of Batangas. It's a huge port but not the biggest port. At medyo masimple po yung pasok doon ng mga containers. And then one airport. And then another port outside Metro Manila.

877
01:19:35,200 --> 01:19:41,880
BOC Commissioner Ariel F. Nepomuceno: Because we have to eventually integrate 17 major ports and 39 sub-ports. We have a total of 56.

878
01:19:41,900 --> 01:19:44,580
BOC Commissioner Ariel F. Nepomuceno: ports to be included in the program.

879
01:19:46,540 --> 01:19:52,460
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: Okay, Usec Ligon, will you also update us with the National Single Window?

880
01:19:52,820 --> 01:20:03,900
DOF Undersecretary Rolando T. Ligon Jr.: Yes, sir. With regards to the National Single Window, we are now in the process of onboarding the different trade-related government agencies.

881
01:20:03,900 --> 01:20:11,900
DOF Undersecretary Rolando T. Ligon Jr.: So, meron akong apat na onboard. This is the National Tobacco Administration, Bureau of Agriculture.

882
01:20:11,900 --> 01:20:20,960
DOF Undersecretary Rolando T. Ligon Jr.: Agriculture and Fisheries, Export Management Bureau, the Bureau of Internal Revenue. And right now, ongoing yung with the Bureau of Customs.

883
01:20:21,740 --> 01:20:30,580
DOF Undersecretary Rolando T. Ligon Jr.: Then in the next two months, we are targeting the onboarding with 22 other agencies.

884
01:20:30,580 --> 01:20:41,680
DOF Undersecretary Rolando T. Ligon Jr.: We are prioritizing yung mga agencies na under the Department of Agriculture, like the National Meat Inspection.

885
01:20:41,900 --> 01:20:50,040
DOF Undersecretary Rolando T. Ligon Jr.: Philippine Coconut Authority, Bureau of Quarantine, Fertilizer and Pesticide Authority.

886
01:20:50,980 --> 01:20:55,860
DOF Undersecretary Rolando T. Ligon Jr.: Yun po yung mga kasunod na isasama sa onboarding.

887
01:20:55,860 --> 01:21:05,740
DOF Undersecretary Rolando T. Ligon Jr.: So, ito pong project na ito, entire project, we're estimating to finish this in one and a half years.

888
01:21:07,040 --> 01:21:10,520
DOF Undersecretary Rolando T. Ligon Jr.: Kompleto na lahat yung iba-ibang agencies na kasama.

889
01:21:10,540 --> 01:21:11,500
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: One and a half years.

890
01:21:11,900 --> 01:21:19,140
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: And that is, but when do you start operating it? Only after one and a half years? Or you can already begin?

891
01:21:19,280 --> 01:21:25,980
DOF Undersecretary Rolando T. Ligon Jr.: Actually po yung naka-onboard na, ano na po yan? Yung pasa na onboard na po, pwede na pong ano yan. Operational na po yan.

892
01:21:26,240 --> 01:21:30,140
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: And what are the onboard agencies?

893
01:21:30,500 --> 01:21:31,420
DOF Undersecretary Rolando T. Ligon Jr.: Yung right now po.

894
01:21:31,420 --> 01:21:34,020
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: You said 40 or 60? What did you say?

895
01:21:34,020 --> 01:21:39,300
DOF Undersecretary Rolando T. Ligon Jr.: Nasa 73 po yung total pag na tapos itong onboarding natin.

896
01:21:39,300 --> 01:21:40,980
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: In one year and a half?

897
01:21:41,140 --> 01:21:41,880
DOF Undersecretary Rolando T. Ligon Jr.: In one year and a half.

898
01:21:41,900 --> 01:22:00,900
DOF Undersecretary Rolando T. Ligon Jr.: In one year and a half po. So, right now po, yung unang na-onboard na is the National Tobacco Administration, Bureau of Agriculture and Fisheries, Export Management Bureau, Bureau of Internal Revenue, and right now, tinatapos na yung sa Bureau of Customs.

899
01:22:06,780 --> 01:22:07,500
DOF Undersecretary Rolando T. Ligon Jr.: Then...

900
01:22:07,500 --> 01:22:10,900
DOF Undersecretary Rolando T. Ligon Jr.: Pero this year po, ang target natin is meron pang...

901
01:22:11,900 --> 01:22:15,000
DOF Undersecretary Rolando T. Ligon Jr.: 22 agencies to be onboarded within the year po.

902
01:22:16,720 --> 01:22:17,200
DOF Undersecretary Rolando T. Ligon Jr.: So...

903
01:22:17,200 --> 01:22:19,840
DOF Undersecretary Rolando T. Ligon Jr.: Until the end of the year po.

904
01:22:20,760 --> 01:22:21,720
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: 22 more. Okay.

905
01:22:21,720 --> 01:22:31,460
DOF Undersecretary Rolando T. Ligon Jr.: Inuuna po natin yung mga bureaus under the Department of Agriculture. Kasi yun po yung merong sensitive po ng mga importation.

906
01:22:31,460 --> 01:22:38,140
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: If I may also add, the reason why the DA is critical here is precisely,

907
01:22:39,020 --> 01:22:41,460
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: we are able to monitor the...

908
01:22:41,900 --> 01:22:51,720
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: entry and, well, the entry of agriculture products through this national single window.

909
01:22:52,600 --> 01:23:00,920
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: And, of course, hindi pa tapos yung ano nila, but this is for DA, yung kanilang first border inspection.

910
01:23:00,920 --> 01:23:07,000
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: We funded that, Mr. Chairman, in the last budget.

911
01:23:08,620 --> 01:23:10,920
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: Walang budget, niligyan natin ng...

912
01:23:10,920 --> 01:23:13,740
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: 1 billion. So, we hope that can be put together.

913
01:23:13,860 --> 01:23:19,440
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: Because, as I was saying then, national single window, Bureau of Customs,

914
01:23:20,320 --> 01:23:21,620
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: the...

915
01:23:21,620 --> 01:23:31,600
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: What was the estimate for the losses in the African swine, the ASF, was about 60, 70 billion.

916
01:23:32,940 --> 01:23:38,140
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: Pretty much brought the local livestock industry to its knees.

917
01:23:38,660 --> 01:23:40,720
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: Simply because, A, we were...

918
01:23:40,920 --> 01:23:46,520
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: unable to monitor the entry of contaminated meat.

919
01:23:47,260 --> 01:23:55,260
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: Now, the other day, I read in the papers that the customs confiscated chicken.

920
01:23:55,260 --> 01:24:04,300
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: Imported chicken that was supposed to be for rendering, meaning susunugin na, di ba?

921
01:24:05,380 --> 01:24:10,260
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: Pero, ang lumalabas, yung rendering agency...

922
01:24:10,920 --> 01:24:17,840
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: Ay, imbis na sunugin o i-render, sirain, ay binenta.

923
01:24:18,860 --> 01:24:19,420
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: Tama?

924
01:24:20,180 --> 01:24:22,280
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: Could you give us an update?

925
01:24:24,340 --> 01:24:27,380
BOC Commissioner Ariel F. Nepomuceno: Actually, you're correct, Your Honor.

926
01:24:27,380 --> 01:24:33,400
BOC Commissioner Ariel F. Nepomuceno: These are apprehended, smuggled chicken meat from Subic.

927
01:24:33,880 --> 01:24:35,380
BOC Commissioner Ariel F. Nepomuceno: Then, they were supposed to be already...

928
01:24:37,800 --> 01:24:40,380
BOC Commissioner Ariel F. Nepomuceno: sa condemnation facilities.

929
01:24:40,920 --> 01:24:42,060
BOC Commissioner Ariel F. Nepomuceno: Somewhere in Bulacan.

930
01:24:42,640 --> 01:24:49,540
BOC Commissioner Ariel F. Nepomuceno: But then, allegedly, there is a transaction that this is supposed to be...

931
01:24:49,540 --> 01:24:52,040
BOC Commissioner Ariel F. Nepomuceno: Those that will be condemned will be sold.

932
01:24:52,780 --> 01:24:55,740
BOC Commissioner Ariel F. Nepomuceno: But we have already ordered the full investigation.

933
01:24:55,740 --> 01:24:58,660
BOC Commissioner Ariel F. Nepomuceno: In fact, we have already...

934
01:24:58,660 --> 01:25:04,320
BOC Commissioner Ariel F. Nepomuceno: I've already ordered the relief of those who are possibly involved in this,

935
01:25:04,380 --> 01:25:07,440
BOC Commissioner Ariel F. Nepomuceno: including the condemnation facility owner.

936
01:25:08,060 --> 01:25:09,560
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: That's about 7 million, no?

937
01:25:10,920 --> 01:25:15,460
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: 7 million pesos worth of smuggled, frozen chicken.

938
01:25:16,100 --> 01:25:16,500
BOC Commissioner Ariel F. Nepomuceno: Yes, sir.

939
01:25:17,140 --> 01:25:20,220
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: Which they were now intending to sell at what?

940
01:25:20,320 --> 01:25:21,840
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: 120 pesos a kilo?

941
01:25:22,580 --> 01:25:23,780
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: In the wet market?

942
01:25:24,420 --> 01:25:24,700
BOC Commissioner Ariel F. Nepomuceno: Yes, sir.

943
01:25:24,760 --> 01:25:27,860
BOC Commissioner Ariel F. Nepomuceno: Actually, naka-apprehend po is the National Bureau of Investigation.

944
01:25:28,240 --> 01:25:29,700
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: Oh, the NBI. That's right.

945
01:25:30,260 --> 01:25:35,640
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: But we also have some rendering issues with the BOC and the DA,

946
01:25:35,640 --> 01:25:40,800
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: which that's why, Secretary, I hope you can support this with Secretary Kiko.

947
01:25:40,920 --> 01:25:45,340
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: When they present their budgets and when you present your budgets in plenary,

948
01:25:45,520 --> 01:25:48,140
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: I hope that you already have that memorandum of agreement

949
01:25:48,140 --> 01:25:51,200
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: between BOC and DA on the rendering.

950
01:25:51,420 --> 01:25:54,520
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: Because we have found out a similar incident.

951
01:25:56,680 --> 01:25:57,540
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: The smuggled...

952
01:25:57,540 --> 01:26:00,000
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: This one is, ano na, BOC.

953
01:26:00,120 --> 01:26:06,680
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: The smuggled meat from Imus was brought to a rendering site,

954
01:26:07,540 --> 01:26:09,100
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: condemnation process.

955
01:26:09,100 --> 01:26:10,100
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: Dinala pa ng...

956
01:26:10,920 --> 01:26:13,720
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: ng Coast Guard.

957
01:26:14,100 --> 01:26:15,260
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: Binantayan ng Coast Guard.

958
01:26:15,380 --> 01:26:21,220
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: Hindi nila iniwanan mula doon sa Cavite, sa Imus ba?

959
01:26:21,320 --> 01:26:22,540
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: O Baco or Imus?

960
01:26:23,260 --> 01:26:24,660
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: Papunta doon sa...

961
01:26:24,660 --> 01:26:25,280
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: Saan ba yun?

962
01:26:26,400 --> 01:26:27,080
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: Paulacan?

963
01:26:28,420 --> 01:26:30,060
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: Tapos pag-alis nung Coast Guard,

964
01:26:32,420 --> 01:26:32,860
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: ni-render.

965
01:26:32,860 --> 01:26:40,780
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: Pero ang lumalabas, inamin mismo ng taga-BAI na binibente yung karni na yun,

966
01:26:40,920 --> 01:26:45,760
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: para gawing pakain sa tilapya.

967
01:26:46,960 --> 01:26:54,160
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: So yung unfit for human consumption na karni na dapat nang i-condemn,

968
01:26:54,280 --> 01:27:01,780
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: binenta sa mga fish pond operator para gawing pakain sa tilapya.

969
01:27:02,840 --> 01:27:05,920
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: At pagkakinain natin yung tilapya...

970
01:27:05,920 --> 01:27:08,920
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: So...

971
01:27:08,920 --> 01:27:10,760
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: It makes me...

972
01:27:10,760 --> 01:27:14,840
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: I wonder, the amount that you said, ng NBI, was 7 million.

973
01:27:15,840 --> 01:27:20,240
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: I wonder how much, if any, pinalusot.

974
01:27:21,200 --> 01:27:21,720
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: Hindi ko alam.

975
01:27:22,760 --> 01:27:28,040
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: But again, with the single window, national single window project,

976
01:27:28,360 --> 01:27:31,100
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: and what you're doing now, we will be able to address this.

977
01:27:31,100 --> 01:27:36,740
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: And, Secretary, yung memorandum of agreement between the DA and the BOC on rendering.

978
01:27:38,200 --> 01:27:39,100
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: So that...

979
01:27:39,840 --> 01:27:40,600
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: That was...

980
01:27:40,760 --> 01:27:42,080
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: It was confiscated by the BOC, eh.

981
01:27:42,700 --> 01:27:43,720
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: Yung sa IMUS, eh.

982
01:27:44,200 --> 01:27:48,800
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: So dapat, pagkadating doon sa condemnation, nandun ng BOC, nandun ng DA,

983
01:27:49,040 --> 01:27:53,840
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: at nagkakaisa na nag-uusap na tama dapat na ma...

984
01:27:53,840 --> 01:27:54,680
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: Go ahead.

985
01:27:57,000 --> 01:28:00,320
BOC Commissioner Ariel F. Nepomuceno: Your Honor, since nandito rin din po tayo doon sa topic ng rendering,

986
01:28:00,920 --> 01:28:04,560
BOC Commissioner Ariel F. Nepomuceno: I'll take advantage to, of course, seek the help of the Senate.

987
01:28:05,540 --> 01:28:08,060
BOC Commissioner Ariel F. Nepomuceno: Ganito po yung sistema po na minana po namin.

988
01:28:08,060 --> 01:28:10,440
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: How much do you need to get the facility?

989
01:28:10,760 --> 01:28:11,240
BOC Commissioner Ariel F. Nepomuceno: Opo.

990
01:28:12,480 --> 01:28:15,180
BOC Commissioner Ariel F. Nepomuceno: Facility sent, ano po, MOE, additional MOE.

991
01:28:15,260 --> 01:28:15,600
BOC Commissioner Ariel F. Nepomuceno: Ganito po.

992
01:28:16,020 --> 01:28:19,440
BOC Commissioner Ariel F. Nepomuceno: Ang dinatan po nating sistema among so many other problems.

993
01:28:20,360 --> 01:28:25,720
BOC Commissioner Ariel F. Nepomuceno: Wala hong budget allotted for the Bureau of Customs to be used for rendering.

994
01:28:26,720 --> 01:28:35,280
BOC Commissioner Ariel F. Nepomuceno: The model is quite peculiar wherein zero budget or zero payment ang naka-allot for the condemnators.

995
01:28:35,680 --> 01:28:39,840
BOC Commissioner Ariel F. Nepomuceno: So we will ask, ba't sila mag-i-interest to do the job?

996
01:28:39,840 --> 01:28:42,900
BOC Commissioner Ariel F. Nepomuceno: So we can speculate, di po ba?

997
01:28:43,360 --> 01:28:44,720
BOC Commissioner Ariel F. Nepomuceno: Kasi hindi naman po sila babayaran.

998
01:28:44,860 --> 01:28:50,520
BOC Commissioner Ariel F. Nepomuceno: Therefore, they're only after what can be salvaged or can be saved or siguro recyclable

999
01:28:50,520 --> 01:28:54,040
BOC Commissioner Ariel F. Nepomuceno: from what is supposed to be going to be condemned or destroyed.

1000
01:28:54,480 --> 01:28:58,180
BOC Commissioner Ariel F. Nepomuceno: So we will seek the help, of course, of Congress and the Senate

1001
01:28:58,180 --> 01:29:03,080
BOC Commissioner Ariel F. Nepomuceno: to support us with at least with the immediate additional MOE

1002
01:29:03,080 --> 01:29:07,100
BOC Commissioner Ariel F. Nepomuceno: for us to be able to finance our own rendering

1003
01:29:07,100 --> 01:29:09,660
BOC Commissioner Ariel F. Nepomuceno: so that we will not be dependent on the condemnation.

1004
01:29:09,820 --> 01:29:12,740
BOC Commissioner Ariel F. Nepomuceno: And we don't know what release on their minds

1005
01:29:12,740 --> 01:29:16,160
BOC Commissioner Ariel F. Nepomuceno: why they are interested to do the rendering job.

1006
01:29:16,700 --> 01:29:17,100
BOC Commissioner Ariel F. Nepomuceno: Isa po yan.

1007
01:29:17,160 --> 01:29:20,000
BOC Commissioner Ariel F. Nepomuceno: With the facility, meron din po kaming nakalista.

1008
01:29:20,200 --> 01:29:22,640
BOC Commissioner Ariel F. Nepomuceno: But of course, we know that this will take time.

1009
01:29:23,200 --> 01:29:27,540
BOC Commissioner Ariel F. Nepomuceno: If at all, 2027 pa natin gagawin to 2028.

1010
01:29:27,640 --> 01:29:29,900
BOC Commissioner Ariel F. Nepomuceno: But we need support po doon sa MOE.

1011
01:29:30,180 --> 01:29:35,960
BOC Commissioner Ariel F. Nepomuceno: Again, for us to fund our condemnation based on our own timing.

1012
01:29:39,820 --> 01:29:44,500
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: Yes, go ahead, sir.

1013
01:29:44,500 --> 01:30:00,000
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: Well, if you'll allow me, Mr. Chair, based on our budget, actually we were cut down on our request, and I will be signing a letter after this briefing to the committee

1014
01:30:00,000 --> 01:30:06,420
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: asking for additional budget of P10 billion for your consideration from the BOC.

1015
01:30:07,040 --> 01:30:11,460
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: And number 8 in that list is the construction of condemnation facilities.

1016
01:30:12,460 --> 01:30:17,220
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: And then the BIR also has a request of about a little over a billion pesos

1017
01:30:17,220 --> 01:30:21,720
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: of necessary budget that they need for their operations.

1018
01:30:21,720 --> 01:30:24,040
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: That was also cut down.

1019
01:30:24,120 --> 01:30:26,400
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: Actually, the amount cut down obviously was much larger.

1020
